                                ;LYTP -- L = the lines to be above the cursor's (H = 0): HL = the start of
                                ; the top line.  WM's line move (LINPSB) would find it, walking back over all
                                ; of them; but HTBLD has walked back already, to the table's first line
                                ; (HTTOPC), and the top line is that one or some lines down from it.  With a
                                ; table that was kept (LYSTP): no lines above, and it is the cursor's line;
                                ; else the top line is the old one, or some lines down from it, and the old
                                ; one is where LYTOP says while the pager has left the text alone.
